<title>AUSTRIA: Buba's Welteke for EMU even with small start group.</title>
<headline>Buba's Welteke for EMU even with small start group.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank council member Ernst Welteke said on Wednesday Europe's planned single currency should get underway even if the starting group were small.</p>
<p>&quot;The main thing is that (the single currency) gets started,&quot; Welteke told reporters during a conference organised by the Austrian National Bank.</p>
<p>Asked if he believed European Economic and Monetary Union should start even with a small number of founding members, he replied: &quot;Yes&quot;. -- Vienna newsroom, +43-1 531 12 254</p>
</text>
